  "geometry": {
    "domain": "Each existing power-ball cell intersected with y >= ground_height. No replacement lattice, fictitious material, or rendering-only clip.",
    "construction": "Re-clip internal wall disks crossing the ground against the ground half-space. Add a floor disk clipped against the owner's real power neighbours. Retain exposed circle arcs and use analytic spherical-sector integration for remaining free caps and cell volume.",
    "moments": "The floor's area, centroid, normal and first surface moment enter volume, velocity gradient, cap second moment, traction and wave-step estimates. Shared internal faces are stored once with opposite orientations.",
    "mass": "Existing extensive mass is conserved. Density uses actual clipped volume; clipping does not discard material mass or reset it to reference density.",
    "kernel": "GPU disk/half-plane clipping, with no contact surface quadrature. Near-zero arc cancellation is avoided using analytic circle chords. The stable area option is enabled only for this new ground adapter; existing unflagged geometry calls retain their previous formula.",
    "abandoned_implementation": "Auxiliary power competitors are mathematically equivalent to a plane but generate forced coincident power boundaries that the existing geometry pipeline mishandled. That implementation was removed. Its failed run logs are retained under output/ale/plane_from_start and plane_stable."
  },
  "mechanics": {
    "floor": "Stationary flat face, zero normal material velocity, zero normal mass flux and zero normal work.",
    "reaction": "P = -sigma_yy - Z*v_y, Z=rho*sound_speed, from the existing acoustic boundary relation. This replaces the curved-surface penalty/dashpot law; it is a physical boundary-model change, not merely an optimization of the old force.",
    "friction": "Cell-constant acoustic tangential relation with Coulomb stick/slip. Tangential dissipation is retained as material heat, giving zero total-energy flux through the stationary floor.",
    "free_surface": "Remaining spherical patches use the existing analytic translating/dilating free-cap solve. Its weak acoustic boundary approximation is retained.",
    "integration": "Existing conservative ALE transport, group agglomeration and SSPRK2 are retained. The unchanged group-selection RHS is reused instead of recomputed."
  },
  "limits": [
    "Tensile acoustic wall predictions stop the trial. Detachment/unloading is not yet a supported boundary transition; the code does not silently impose adhesive contact.",
    "This is the experimental sphere-boundary FV adaptation, not a validated reproduction of a published complete solid ALE scheme.",
    "Source/work balance checks do not prove constitutive accuracy, thermodynamic consistency, time convergence or robustness of full landing.",
    "Saved frame files include ground_clipped and ground_height. Renderers that draw uncut spheres must explicitly honour these fields before interpreting below-ground sphere parts as physical penetration.",
    "Physical substeps and elapsed cost must be reported. A first post-contact output frame is not the complete 0.625 second landing."
